  "why": "The statement asks for the values of the van der Waerden numbers, a table quantified over all r and k (and, on the article's scope, off-diagonal entries). Each exact value determined is therefore a case, and every growth estimate is a bound. All exact values (W(3,3), W(2,5), W(2,6), W(3,4), Ahmed's off-diagonal values) predate the snapshot. W(4,3) is undated and Karki's 2024 value cannot be placed relative to 26 January, so both get null. After the snapshot nothing determines a value. Campos-Fox-Schildkraut, Fox-Hunter, Cao (w(3,k) is an off-diagonal entry the article tabulates) and the vdw-records W(3,19..25) lower bounds all move bounds on table quantities. The gap results on W(k+1)-W(k) (AlphaProof Nexus, Sothanaphan) answer a different question about differences and are variants; the paper's own table calls 138 a variant. The Lean re-verification of the 1978 W(2,5)=178 is a formalisation of a known result, so it scores none. The Hunter talk has no written argument and also scores none. For AI roles: Campos et al. say the model generated the colouring and a proof, and the authors rewrote the proof drawing on it. Since the construction that the result rests on is the model's, that is generated rather than assisted. vdw-records says everything was produced by Claude, so it is generated. On the variant rows, the forum co-credit to GPT-5.4 is thin but names the model as co-producer of the refinement, so it is assisted.",
